{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":1,"id":"deferred-acquisition-review-2026-10-07","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Deferred acquisition review, 2026-10-07"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Scope: PR #2060 ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"issue-2023-network-on-subscriber"},{"type":"text","value":") at "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"19588268c"},{"type":"text","value":", reviewed by\nan external high-effort code review. The repair commit that adds this record\nsits on top of that revision. Owner:\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"packages/db/tests/live-query-deferred-acquisition-oracle.test.ts"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"law","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Law"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Normative law 15 in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"packages/db/src/query/live/ARCHITECTURE.md"},{"type":"text","value":". Authority:\nthe maintainer's decision that a live query starts no network work until it\nhas a subscriber or a preload, with preload counting and eager sources\nincluded. This review sharpened the formulation: the subscriber must ask for\ndata, a subscriber that survives cleanup still counts, and a read that waits\nfor readiness counts as a preload."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"findings-and-evidence","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Findings and evidence"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Finding"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Kind"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Evidence"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Outcome"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A source status change restarts deferred demand"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defect"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"New "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"peer"},{"type":"text","value":" command: a peer that starts an idle on-demand source made the live query acquire, 4 cases RED at the acquisition-count assertion"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Guard in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"restartDetachedDemands"},{"type":"text","value":"; removing it alone fails the same 4"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A truncate reloads deferred demand"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defect"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"New "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"truncate"},{"type":"text","value":" command: 8 cases RED at the acquisition-count assertion"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Guard in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"handleTruncate"},{"type":"text","value":"; removing it alone fails the same 8"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cleanup resets the flag while an acquiring subscriber survives"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defect and formulation"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pinned block: 4 on-demand cases RED, no acquisition after restart, status stuck at "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"loading"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cleanup keeps the flag when a surviving subscription does not defer. \"Always reset\" fails the block; \"any surviving subscriber\" fails the deferring-survivor control"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A deferring subscription raises the source's subscriber count"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Concept question"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A Query Collection probe: the count went 0 to 1, but no refetch happened"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No change; harm not reproduced. Whether "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"subscriberCount"},{"type":"text","value":" should count deferring subscriptions stays open"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A resume that throws leaves later sources deferred"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mechanism confirmed"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Probe: the subscribe throws the first source's error, the live query enters "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"error"},{"type":"text","value":", and the second source stays idle"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No change. The live query has already failed, the deferral is per subscription so another reader starts the source itself, and the remaining trigger is a throwing listener, a contract breach"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toArrayWhenReady()"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stateWhenReady()"},{"type":"text","value":" never resume"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defect"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pinned block: 2 cases RED, no acquisition after the read"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The early-return branch marks a preload"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The first commit is loading under the async resume"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Accepted design"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Maintainer decision: loading first unless the collection is preloaded"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No change"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The changeset is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"patch"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Accepted design"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Maintainer decision"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No change"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A stale comment promises a ready first commit"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Maintainability"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Source inspection, React and Svelte"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Comments rewritten"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The deferral expression is duplicated"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Maintainability"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Source inspection"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"One helper"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"preloaded-collection-first-paint"},{"type":"text","value":" previously rejected the \"preload does not\ncount\" mutant only by timing out. It now bounds the preload, and the mutant\nfails the assertion "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"the preload settles"},{"type":"text","value":" in React, Vue, and Svelte."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The mutants above were designed after reading the tests, so they are a\nself-review of this author's coverage, not an independent mutant gap hunt."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"second-review-at-c2fe18d21","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Second review, at "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"c2fe18d21"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A medium code review raised ten findings. Each claim was probed on that\nrevision before any change."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Finding"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Kind"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Evidence"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Outcome"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A deferring subscription raises the source's subscriber count, so a Query Collection refetches"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defect, open"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"With the reviewer's precondition (the last direct subscriber left first), a live query with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"startSync: true"},{"type":"text","value":" and no subscriber raised the count from 0 to 1 and the Query Collection fetched again. The first review's probe had no prior subscriber"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Maintainer decision: they count only subscribers that ask for data, while garbage collection still counts every subscription. A pinned oracle block and a Query Collection test fail without the change; ten tests that read "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"subscriberCount"},{"type":"text","value":" to watch an abandoned render or orphan hold its source now observe the hold another way: db tests read the retention count, and React tests give the source a 1 ms "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gcTime"},{"type":"text","value":" and check that it survives while held and is reclaimed after"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A resume that throws strands the other sources and makes "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"preload()"},{"type":"text","value":" throw"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defect"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pinned block: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"preload()"},{"type":"text","value":" threw synchronously instead of returning a rejected promise"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Listeners all run before the first error is rethrown; the preload entry points reject. Each half fails the block alone"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A failed resume clears the subscription's deferring flag"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defect by source inspection"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Observable only when the failing source is itself a live query that is later cleaned up; no runtime witness"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The source starts before the flag clears"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A truncate with retained stale rows stalls publication"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Refuted at the precondition"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Retained stale rows come only from source cleanup, which puts the dependent live query in terminal error first"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No change"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A cleaned-up Suspense collection gets no in-render preload"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pre-existing defect"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The rerender showed no rows on this PR and on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"main"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The in-render preload covers "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cleaned-up"},{"type":"text","value":"; the new React witness fails without it"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The first-value helper accepts any not-ready value"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Weak assertion"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Source inspection"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The not-ready value is now exact: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"loading"},{"type":"text","value":" when the hook started the collection, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"idle"},{"type":"text","value":" for a supplied window it adjusts first"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hasSubscriberOrPreload()"},{"type":"text","value":" falls back to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Refuted: reachable"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A non-null assertion failed 8 scheduler tests that drive the builder without its Collection"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fallback kept, with a comment naming where it is reached"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pooled "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"preload()"},{"type":"text","value":" leaves the partition deferring"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Refuted at the precondition"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The partition unsubscribes when its source's cleanup starts, so no survivor is miscounted"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No change"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The change manager special-cases live-query Collections"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Design"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Source inspection"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No change; a config-level capability would add surface for one caller"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A test comment is out of order"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Maintainability"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Source inspection"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fixed"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"third-review-at-9fb2d810a","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Third review, at "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"9fb2d810a"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Finding"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Kind"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Evidence"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Outcome"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A failed source start cannot be retried in the same sync run"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Refuted under the accepted contract"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pinned block: the failed start puts the source and its live query in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"error"},{"type":"text","value":"; cleanup and a new preload start the source again and load it"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No change; the block keeps the supported recovery path"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A Suspense render could hang after a failed start"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Refuted at the premise"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The live query does enter "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"error"},{"type":"text","value":", so "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useLiveSuspenseQuery"},{"type":"text","value":" surfaces it"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No change"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A subscriber or preload during a source's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"subscribe()"},{"type":"text","value":" is missed"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defect"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A handler on the outer live query's own status never ran inside the window. A status handler on an inner live query did: subscribing to the inner query starts it, and a handler that preloads or subscribes to the outer query left it at "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"loading"},{"type":"text","value":" with no acquisition. Pinned block, both requests RED"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"After registering its listener, the source subscription resumes at once when a request already arrived"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A ready read returns partial local rows"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pre-existing contract"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Both reads resolve at once when the Collection holds rows; they now also request the rest"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No change; waiting instead would change every Collection's ready reads"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A preload rejected during cleanup leaves the flag set"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Refuted at the precondition"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A live query's cleanup completes before the next call, so the preload was accepted and the restart acquired nothing extra"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No change"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pooled "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"preload()"},{"type":"text","value":" does not resume the partition"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Refuted"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pooled views serve eager sources only, whose demand never detaches; the oracle's \"preload after build\" cases pass"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No change"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Patch changeset, layering, the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"?? true"},{"type":"text","value":" fallback"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Already decided or recorded above"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No change"}]}]]}],"headings":[{"id":"deferred-acquisition-review-2026-10-07","text":"Deferred acquisition review, 2026-10-07","level":1},{"id":"law","text":"Law","level":2},{"id":"findings-and-evidence","text":"Findings and evidence","level":2},{"id":"second-review-at-c2fe18d21","text":"Second review, at c2fe18d21","level":2},{"id":"third-review-at-9fb2d810a","text":"Third review, at 9fb2d810a","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"# Deferred acquisition review, 2026-10-07\n\nScope: PR #2060 (`issue-2023-network-on-subscriber`) at `19588268c`, reviewed by\nan external high-effort code review. The repair commit that adds this record\nsits on top of that revision. Owner:\n`packages/db/tests/live-query-deferred-acquisition-oracle.test.ts`.\n\n## Law\n\nNormative law 15 in `packages/db/src/query/live/ARCHITECTURE.md`. Authority:\nthe maintainer's decision that a live query starts no network work until it\nhas a subscriber or a preload, with preload counting and eager sources\nincluded. This review sharpened the formulation: the subscriber must ask for\ndata, a subscriber that survives cleanup still counts, and a read that waits\nfor readiness counts as a preload.\n\n## Findings and evidence\n\n| Finding | Kind | Evidence | Outcome |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| A source status change restarts deferred demand | Defect | New `peer` command: a peer that starts an idle on-demand source made the live query acquire, 4 cases RED at the acquisition-count assertion | Guard in `restartDetachedDemands`; removing it alone fails the same 4 |\n| A truncate reloads deferred demand | Defect | New `truncate` command: 8 cases RED at the acquisition-count assertion | Guard in `handleTruncate`; removing it alone fails the same 8 |\n| Cleanup resets the flag while an acquiring subscriber survives | Defect and formulation | Pinned block: 4 on-demand cases RED, no acquisition after restart, status stuck at `loading` | Cleanup keeps the flag when a surviving subscription does not defer. \"Always reset\" fails the block; \"any surviving subscriber\" fails the deferring-survivor control |\n| A deferring subscription raises the source's subscriber count | Concept question | A Query Collection probe: the count went 0 to 1, but no refetch happened | No change; harm not reproduced. Whether `subscriberCount` should count deferring subscriptions stays open |\n| A resume that throws leaves later sources deferred | Mechanism confirmed | Probe: the subscribe throws the first source's error, the live query enters `error`, and the second source stays idle | No change. The live query has already failed, the deferral is per subscription so another reader starts the source itself, and the remaining trigger is a throwing listener, a contract breach |\n| `toArrayWhenReady()` / `stateWhenReady()` never resume | Defect | Pinned block: 2 cases RED, no acquisition after the read | The early-return branch marks a preload |\n| The first commit is loading under the async resume | Accepted design | Maintainer decision: loading first unless the collection is preloaded | No change |\n| The changeset is `patch` | Accepted design | Maintainer decision | No change |\n| A stale comment promises a ready first commit | Maintainability | Source inspection, React and Svelte | Comments rewritten |\n| The deferral expression is duplicated | Maintainability | Source inspection | One helper |\n\n`preloaded-collection-first-paint` previously rejected the \"preload does not\ncount\" mutant only by timing out. It now bounds the preload, and the mutant\nfails the assertion `the preload settles` in React, Vue, and Svelte.\n\nThe mutants above were designed after reading the tests, so they are a\nself-review of this author's coverage, not an independent mutant gap hunt.\n\n## Second review, at `c2fe18d21`\n\nA medium code review raised ten findings. Each claim was probed on that\nrevision before any change.\n\n| Finding | Kind | Evidence | Outcome |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| A deferring subscription raises the source's subscriber count, so a Query Collection refetches | Defect, open | With the reviewer's precondition (the last direct subscriber left first), a live query with `startSync: true` and no subscriber raised the count from 0 to 1 and the Query Collection fetched again. The first review's probe had no prior subscriber | Maintainer decision: they count only subscribers that ask for data, while garbage collection still counts every subscription. A pinned oracle block and a Query Collection test fail without the change; ten tests that read `subscriberCount` to watch an abandoned render or orphan hold its source now observe the hold another way: db tests read the retention count, and React tests give the source a 1 ms `gcTime` and check that it survives while held and is reclaimed after |\n| A resume that throws strands the other sources and makes `preload()` throw | Defect | Pinned block: `preload()` threw synchronously instead of returning a rejected promise | Listeners all run before the first error is rethrown; the preload entry points reject. Each half fails the block alone |\n| A failed resume clears the subscription's deferring flag | Defect by source inspection | Observable only when the failing source is itself a live query that is later cleaned up; no runtime witness | The source starts before the flag clears |\n| A truncate with retained stale rows stalls publication | Refuted at the precondition | Retained stale rows come only from source cleanup, which puts the dependent live query in terminal error first | No change |\n| A cleaned-up Suspense collection gets no in-render preload | Pre-existing defect | The rerender showed no rows on this PR and on `main` | The in-render preload covers `cleaned-up`; the new React witness fails without it |\n| The first-value helper accepts any not-ready value | Weak assertion | Source inspection | The not-ready value is now exact: `loading` when the hook started the collection, `idle` for a supplied window it adjusts first |\n| `hasSubscriberOrPreload()` falls back to `true` | Refuted: reachable | A non-null assertion failed 8 scheduler tests that drive the builder without its Collection | Fallback kept, with a comment naming where it is reached |\n| Pooled `preload()` leaves the partition deferring | Refuted at the precondition | The partition unsubscribes when its source's cleanup starts, so no survivor is miscounted | No change |\n| The change manager special-cases live-query Collections | Design | Source inspection | No change; a config-level capability would add surface for one caller |\n| A test comment is out of order | Maintainability | Source inspection | Fixed |\n\n## Third review, at `9fb2d810a`\n\n| Finding | Kind | Evidence | Outcome |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| A failed source start cannot be retried in the same sync run | Refuted under the accepted contract | Pinned block: the failed start puts the source and its live query in `error`; cleanup and a new preload start the source again and load it | No change; the block keeps the supported recovery path |\n| A Suspense render could hang after a failed start | Refuted at the premise | The live query does enter `error`, so `useLiveSuspenseQuery` surfaces it | No change |\n| A subscriber or preload during a source's `subscribe()` is missed | Defect | A handler on the outer live query's own status never ran inside the window. A status handler on an inner live query did: subscribing to the inner query starts it, and a handler that preloads or subscribes to the outer query left it at `loading` with no acquisition. Pinned block, both requests RED | After registering its listener, the source subscription resumes at once when a request already arrived |\n| A ready read returns partial local rows | Pre-existing contract | Both reads resolve at once when the Collection holds rows; they now also request the rest | No change; waiting instead would change every Collection's ready reads |\n| A preload rejected during cleanup leaves the flag set | Refuted at the precondition | A live query's cleanup completes before the next call, so the preload was accepted and the restart acquired nothing extra | No change |\n| Pooled `preload()` does not resume the partition | Refuted | Pooled views serve eager sources only, whose demand never detaches; the oracle's \"preload after build\" cases pass | No change |\n| Patch changeset, layering, the `?? true` fallback | Already decided or recorded above | | No change |\n","originalRawMarkdown":"# Deferred acquisition review, 2026-10-07\n\nScope: PR #2060 (`issue-2023-network-on-subscriber`) at `19588268c`, reviewed by\nan external high-effort code review. The repair commit that adds this record\nsits on top of that revision. Owner:\n`packages/db/tests/live-query-deferred-acquisition-oracle.test.ts`.\n\n## Law\n\nNormative law 15 in `packages/db/src/query/live/ARCHITECTURE.md`. Authority:\nthe maintainer's decision that a live query starts no network work until it\nhas a subscriber or a preload, with preload counting and eager sources\nincluded. This review sharpened the formulation: the subscriber must ask for\ndata, a subscriber that survives cleanup still counts, and a read that waits\nfor readiness counts as a preload.\n\n## Findings and evidence\n\n| Finding | Kind | Evidence | Outcome |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| A source status change restarts deferred demand | Defect | New `peer` command: a peer that starts an idle on-demand source made the live query acquire, 4 cases RED at the acquisition-count assertion | Guard in `restartDetachedDemands`; removing it alone fails the same 4 |\n| A truncate reloads deferred demand | Defect | New `truncate` command: 8 cases RED at the acquisition-count assertion | Guard in `handleTruncate`; removing it alone fails the same 8 |\n| Cleanup resets the flag while an acquiring subscriber survives | Defect and formulation | Pinned block: 4 on-demand cases RED, no acquisition after restart, status stuck at `loading` | Cleanup keeps the flag when a surviving subscription does not defer. \"Always reset\" fails the block; \"any surviving subscriber\" fails the deferring-survivor control |\n| A deferring subscription raises the source's subscriber count | Concept question | A Query Collection probe: the count went 0 to 1, but no refetch happened | No change; harm not reproduced. Whether `subscriberCount` should count deferring subscriptions stays open |\n| A resume that throws leaves later sources deferred | Mechanism confirmed | Probe: the subscribe throws the first source's error, the live query enters `error`, and the second source stays idle | No change. The live query has already failed, the deferral is per subscription so another reader starts the source itself, and the remaining trigger is a throwing listener, a contract breach |\n| `toArrayWhenReady()` / `stateWhenReady()` never resume | Defect | Pinned block: 2 cases RED, no acquisition after the read | The early-return branch marks a preload |\n| The first commit is loading under the async resume | Accepted design | Maintainer decision: loading first unless the collection is preloaded | No change |\n| The changeset is `patch` | Accepted design | Maintainer decision | No change |\n| A stale comment promises a ready first commit | Maintainability | Source inspection, React and Svelte | Comments rewritten |\n| The deferral expression is duplicated | Maintainability | Source inspection | One helper |\n\n`preloaded-collection-first-paint` previously rejected the \"preload does not\ncount\" mutant only by timing out. It now bounds the preload, and the mutant\nfails the assertion `the preload settles` in React, Vue, and Svelte.\n\nThe mutants above were designed after reading the tests, so they are a\nself-review of this author's coverage, not an independent mutant gap hunt.\n\n## Second review, at `c2fe18d21`\n\nA medium code review raised ten findings. Each claim was probed on that\nrevision before any change.\n\n| Finding | Kind | Evidence | Outcome |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| A deferring subscription raises the source's subscriber count, so a Query Collection refetches | Defect, open | With the reviewer's precondition (the last direct subscriber left first), a live query with `startSync: true` and no subscriber raised the count from 0 to 1 and the Query Collection fetched again. The first review's probe had no prior subscriber | Maintainer decision: they count only subscribers that ask for data, while garbage collection still counts every subscription. A pinned oracle block and a Query Collection test fail without the change; ten tests that read `subscriberCount` to watch an abandoned render or orphan hold its source now observe the hold another way: db tests read the retention count, and React tests give the source a 1 ms `gcTime` and check that it survives while held and is reclaimed after |\n| A resume that throws strands the other sources and makes `preload()` throw | Defect | Pinned block: `preload()` threw synchronously instead of returning a rejected promise | Listeners all run before the first error is rethrown; the preload entry points reject. Each half fails the block alone |\n| A failed resume clears the subscription's deferring flag | Defect by source inspection | Observable only when the failing source is itself a live query that is later cleaned up; no runtime witness | The source starts before the flag clears |\n| A truncate with retained stale rows stalls publication | Refuted at the precondition | Retained stale rows come only from source cleanup, which puts the dependent live query in terminal error first | No change |\n| A cleaned-up Suspense collection gets no in-render preload | Pre-existing defect | The rerender showed no rows on this PR and on `main` | The in-render preload covers `cleaned-up`; the new React witness fails without it |\n| The first-value helper accepts any not-ready value | Weak assertion | Source inspection | The not-ready value is now exact: `loading` when the hook started the collection, `idle` for a supplied window it adjusts first |\n| `hasSubscriberOrPreload()` falls back to `true` | Refuted: reachable | A non-null assertion failed 8 scheduler tests that drive the builder without its Collection | Fallback kept, with a comment naming where it is reached |\n| Pooled `preload()` leaves the partition deferring | Refuted at the precondition | The partition unsubscribes when its source's cleanup starts, so no survivor is miscounted | No change |\n| The change manager special-cases live-query Collections | Design | Source inspection | No change; a config-level capability would add surface for one caller |\n| A test comment is out of order | Maintainability | Source inspection | Fixed |\n\n## Third review, at `9fb2d810a`\n\n| Finding | Kind | Evidence | Outcome |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| A failed source start cannot be retried in the same sync run | Refuted under the accepted contract | Pinned block: the failed start puts the source and its live query in `error`; cleanup and a new preload start the source again and load it | No change; the block keeps the supported recovery path |\n| A Suspense render could hang after a failed start | Refuted at the premise | The live query does enter `error`, so `useLiveSuspenseQuery` surfaces it | No change |\n| A subscriber or preload during a source's `subscribe()` is missed | Defect | A handler on the outer live query's own status never ran inside the window. A status handler on an inner live query did: subscribing to the inner query starts it, and a handler that preloads or subscribes to the outer query left it at `loading` with no acquisition. Pinned block, both requests RED | After registering its listener, the source subscription resumes at once when a request already arrived |\n| A ready read returns partial local rows | Pre-existing contract | Both reads resolve at once when the Collection holds rows; they now also request the rest | No change; waiting instead would change every Collection's ready reads |\n| A preload rejected during cleanup leaves the flag set | Refuted at the precondition | A live query's cleanup completes before the next call, so the preload was accepted and the restart acquired nothing extra | No change |\n| Pooled `preload()` does not resume the partition | Refuted | Pooled views serve eager sources only, whose demand never detaches; the oracle's \"preload after build\" cases pass | No change |\n| Patch changeset, layering, the `?? true` fallback | Already decided or recorded above | | No change |\n"}
